    "# Sinusoids, from math to code\n",
    "\n",
    "**Goal:** Generate a simple sinusoidal signal (sine wave), plot it, and save the figure.  \n",
    "We will use **NumPy** to generate the data and **Matplotlib** to plot the curve.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Mathematical background\n",
    "\n",
    "A sinusoid is defined as:\n",
    "\n",
    "\\[\n",
    "s(t) = A \\cdot \\sin(2 \\pi f(t) + \\varphi)\n", #use some "$" to make it nice
    "\\]\n",
    "\n",
    "where:\n",
    "- \\( A \\) = amplitude\n",
    "- \\( f \\) = frequency (Hz)\n",
    "- \\( t \\) = time (s)\n",
    "- \\( \\varphi \\) = phase (rad)\n",
    "\n",
    "For this draft version, we will use:\n",
    "- Amplitude \\( A = 1 \\)\n",
    "- Frequency \\( f = 1 \\) Hz\n",
    "- Phase \\( \\varphi = 0 \\)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 45,
   "id": "0d0181ec",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x400 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "# ----------------------------\n",
    "# Generate the time array: 1000 values between 0 and 1 second\n",
    "# ----------------------------\n",
    "t = np.linspace(0, 1, 1000)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ----------------------------\n",
    "# Generate the sine and cosine waves\n",
    "# ----------------------------\n",
    "sine_signal = np.sin(2 * np.pi * t)       # sine wave: s(t) = sin(2πt)\n",
    "cosine_signal = np.cos(2 * np.pi * t)     # cosine wave: c(t) = cos(2πt)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ----------------------------\n",
    "# Plot signals with two y-axes\n",
    "# ----------------------------\n",
    "fig, ax1 = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 4))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot sine on the left y-axis\n",
    "line1, = ax1.plot(t, sine_signal, 'b-', label=\"sin(2πt)\")\n",
    "ax1.set_xlabel(\"Time (s)\")\n",
    "ax1.set_ylabel(\"Sine Amplitude\", color='b')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create second y-axis for cosine\n",
    "ax2 = ax1.twinx()\n",
    "line2, = ax2.plot(t, cosine_signal, linestyle='-', color='orange', label=\"cos(2πt)\")  # <-- color fixed\n",
    "ax2.set_ylabel(\"Cosine Amplitude\", color='orange')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Combine legends from both axes\n",
    "lines = [line1, line2]\n",
    "ax1.legend(lines, [line.get_label() for line in lines], loc='upper right')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.title(\"Sine and Cosine Signals with Two Y-Axes\")\n",
    "plt.grid(True)\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# ----------------------------\n",
    "# Save the figure as PDF\n",
    "# ----------------------------\n",
    "fig.savefig(\"sine_cos_signals.pdf\", dpi=300)\n",
    "plt.close()\n"
   ]
  },
